wh40k-footfall-lore-marisveyra-1-choice = Who does your office serve?
wh40k-footfall-lore-marisveyra-1-reply = The Rogue Trader dynasty's administration. The Warrant opens distant routes to the captain; my office assembles the people, supplies and obligations needed to sail them. The seal looks magnificent. Beneath it is usually a list of what someone forgot to load.
wh40k-footfall-lore-marisveyra-2-choice = Why do returning crews matter so much to you?
wh40k-footfall-lore-marisveyra-2-reply = Footfall lives on arriving ships. To me, a return is more than tonnage: people will collect their wages again and argue about rations. I rather like those arguments. A silent payroll after a lost voyage is much harder to read.

wh40k-footfall-lore-hestvarn-1-choice = How does supply fit into a Rogue Trader's operation?
wh40k-footfall-lore-hestvarn-1-reply = The trading office counts revenue, the captain counts discoveries, and I count the crates that make both possible. Respectfully staring at a Warrant does not turn it into oxygen reserves. Supplies and manifests first, glorious expedition speeches afterwards.
wh40k-footfall-lore-hestvarn-2-choice = What makes a good porter?
wh40k-footfall-lore-hestvarn-2-reply = Someone who leaves both the goods and their record findable. On Footfall crates often travel more confidently than their owners, especially without labels. Packing is half the job; preventing the next shift from declaring it mysterious inheritance is the other half.

wh40k-footfall-lore-avelinequill-1-choice = What is a Navigator House?
wh40k-footfall-lore-avelinequill-1-reply = Our Houses inherit a particular gift: a Navigator can perceive the currents of the warp and guide a ship through them. Captains contract with Houses rather than merely buy better charts. A House keeps routes, names and debts. Names sometimes change more often than debts.
wh40k-footfall-lore-avelinequill-2-choice = Why will you not promise a safe passage?
wh40k-footfall-lore-avelinequill-2-reply = Charts record experience; the warp need not conform to it. The Astronomican helps us find our bearings but does not remove a passage's dangers. I offer judgement and experience, not obedience from the void. Captains favour the latter wording until the first storm.

wh40k-footfall-lore-omicronkhepra-1-choice = Why is repair sacred service to the Mechanicus?
wh40k-footfall-lore-omicronkhepra-1-reply = The Machine God is honoured through knowledge and the proper work of mechanisms. Ritual preserves the procedure; records preserve its continuity. Pray but skip checking the contacts, and you have shortened more than the rite: you have shortened the relay's life.
wh40k-footfall-lore-omicronkhepra-2-choice = What do you do here besides issue assignments?
wh40k-footfall-lore-omicronkhepra-2-reply = The shield core, energy storage, atmosphere and data networks need coordinated maintenance. Failure often begins at a small node everyone considers someone else's responsibility. My duty is to keep that node from becoming the station's last functioning device.

wh40k-footfall-lore-seraholt-1-choice = What are chartered medicae?
wh40k-footfall-lore-seraholt-1-reply = Our charter sets duties and responsibility, not a special form of circulation. We receive dockworkers, crews and expedition casualties, keep records and try not to lose patients between shifts. A seal belongs on a document. It does very little on a wound.
wh40k-footfall-lore-seraholt-2-choice = How has Footfall changed your work?
wh40k-footfall-lore-seraholt-2-reply = Someone can survive the void here and then be injured by their own crate at the docks. I do not sort patients by the grandeur of their story. Condition first, story second. The story often explains why they dread a simple dressing.

wh40k-footfall-lore-odranpell-1-choice = How do independent merchants make a living?
wh40k-footfall-lore-odranpell-1-reply = Without a dynasty behind us, our name matters. A Rogue Trader may bring a haul, but the local buyer will return tomorrow. I separate an object's story from what can actually be checked. A legend weighs very little; its markup can be quite heavy.
wh40k-footfall-lore-odranpell-2-choice = What find would you refuse?
wh40k-footfall-lore-odranpell-2-reply = One the seller will not name and keeps insisting must stay shut. Some things are rarities, others are someone else's troubles in an attractive case. On Footfall spotting the difference matters more than being first to display it.

wh40k-footfall-lore-kappaspanner-1-choice = Do you serve the Mechanicus or trade independently?
wh40k-footfall-lore-kappaspanner-1-reply = I run an independent ship-supply concern, not a magos's office speaking for the whole Cult. Knowing tools and respecting machinery are useful behind a counter too. My agreements carry my own seal; fortunately, spare-part dimensions do not change with it.
wh40k-footfall-lore-kappaspanner-2-choice = Why are vending machines not enough for expeditions?
wh40k-footfall-lore-kappaspanner-2-reply = A machine dispenses what someone loaded into it. A merchant can also ask where you are going and what needs repairing. Sometimes the buyer picked a tool for its impressive name. Then I rescue their purse first and the airlock afterwards.

wh40k-footfall-lore-vennors-1-choice = Why does a casino thrive here?
wh40k-footfall-lore-vennors-1-reply = People return to Footfall with money and accounts of extraordinary luck. Casey's casino lets them see how much luck survived the voyage. I welcome guests and watch the room. Judging by their stories, every other visitor ought to own the place by now.
wh40k-footfall-lore-vennors-2-choice = What do you consider a bad wager?
wh40k-footfall-lore-vennors-2-reply = One that leaves someone without a bed or passage on their next voyage. Not the most exciting casino sentiment, I know. Still, I prefer a visitor who can return tomorrow to the hero of a single evening.

wh40k-footfall-lore-brannakest-1-choice = What feeds the people keeping Footfall running?
wh40k-footfall-lore-brannakest-1-reply = Whatever they can eat between shifts. A docker needs lunch, an expedition needs rations, and a foreman sometimes needs a reason to seat the crew together. No grand order owns my canteen. Stop feeding people and the port's grandeur soon grows irritable.
wh40k-footfall-lore-brannakest-2-choice = Why ask about the journey?
wh40k-footfall-lore-brannakest-2-reply = A fine lunch and food for the road are different jobs. I ask how many people are going and what they will carry. Everyone claims to eat very little. Then 'very little' turns out to mean another hungry person every two hours.

wh40k-footfall-lore-marasevrin-1-choice = What place does your shop have in the port?
wh40k-footfall-lore-marasevrin-1-reply = An independent counter lives on returning customers. I dress those just off a ship and those trying to look as though they have never seen the lower docks. The latter get a sterner collar. The former get something they can actually wear.
wh40k-footfall-lore-marasevrin-2-choice = Can clothes really help someone settle in here?
wh40k-footfall-lore-marasevrin-2-reply = Some want to change what they wore throughout a hard voyage. Others need to look presentable before a new employer. Cloth cannot erase the past, but it can help choose how the next conversation begins. Debts, sadly, recognise a customer even in a new coat.

wh40k-footfall-lore-dorianbale-1-choice = Whom does a licensed arms dealer represent?
wh40k-footfall-lore-dorianbale-1-reply = I operate under the trading concern's Imperial authorisation. An arms supplier must know a batch's origin and sale conditions as well as its price. My counter is not an Arbites post, but lacking a badge does not make me fond of unrecorded deals.
wh40k-footfall-lore-dorianbale-2-choice = What do you think of glory seekers?
wh40k-footfall-lore-dorianbale-2-reply = I prefer buyers who know why they need a particular weapon and who will check the equipment before departure. Someone promising to defeat everything with one purchase usually forgets supplies. I do not sell glory. It too often comes back damaged.

wh40k-footfall-lore-edricmoss-1-choice = Why help market visitors?
wh40k-footfall-lore-edricmoss-1-reply = Footfall's market connects ships with people staying in port. If a newcomer leaves baffled, both sides lose. I explain the console procedure so a deal begins with understanding and an argument at least begins with one clear reason.
wh40k-footfall-lore-edricmoss-2-choice = What do people confuse most often here?
wh40k-footfall-lore-edricmoss-2-reply = A find's price and the value of their memory of finding it. The console did not join your heroic voyage; it values the submitted item. Tell the story later over a table. A good story might earn a drink, which is another kind of settlement.

wh40k-footfall-lore-borsgrant-1-choice = Why sell construction materials?
wh40k-footfall-lore-borsgrant-1-reply = An independent merchant need not display curiosities. Footfall is constantly patched and rebuilt; people need ordinary sheets and planks rather than jewels. They have no splendid tale. After the job you get a wall instead of another retelling.
wh40k-footfall-lore-borsgrant-2-choice = Do you trust the builder or the customer more?
wh40k-footfall-lore-borsgrant-2-reply = Whoever calculated the quantity beforehand. An unprepared builder wants another batch; an unprepared customer insists the last one should have sufficed. I sell to both, labelling the bundles so at least the material stays out of their argument.

wh40k-footfall-lore-neraquinn-1-choice = Why keep a shop for everyday things in a port?
wh40k-footfall-lore-neraquinn-1-reply = Between great expeditions someone still cleans, carries belongings and makes a place to live. I run an independent shop rather than represent a vast depot. My customers usually want an easier day, not a place in a chronicle.
wh40k-footfall-lore-neraquinn-2-choice = What surprises customers most?
wh40k-footfall-lore-neraquinn-2-reply = A useful thing can look completely dull. After a voyage people seek the extraordinary, then return for the most ordinary item. On Footfall that is a good sign: someone is thinking about tomorrow rather than only yesterday's adventure.

wh40k-footfall-lore-kassmarket-1-choice = Do you work for the Kasballica?
wh40k-footfall-lore-kassmarket-1-reply = I trade at my own risk. The port has plenty of middlemen, including Kasballica people, but knowing someone does not make me their representative. You buy goods, not the right to use another person's name. A name can cost more than the whole batch.
wh40k-footfall-lore-kassmarket-2-choice = Why stand in a corridor instead of a pavilion?
wh40k-footfall-lore-kassmarket-2-reply = A pavilion attracts browsers; a corridor attracts people who know what they want. I prefer the latter conversation. Footfall has signs enough; some deals benefit more from a short talk. A quiet voice does not promise an absence of risk.

wh40k-footfall-lore-ivomercer-1-choice = Why is the bar always busy?
wh40k-footfall-lore-ivomercer-1-reply = Dockworkers finish shifts, crews await passage, and returnees want somewhere to sit without a foreman's order. We are simply Footfall people, but without places like this the port becomes one long corridor to the next job. At least I put glasses in that corridor.
wh40k-footfall-lore-ivomercer-2-choice = Do people tell you true stories?
wh40k-footfall-lore-ivomercer-2-reply = More often early in the evening. Later the same voyage acquires another storm and another rescued captain. I remember people, not records. I want the teller back tomorrow; they can revise the tale then.

wh40k-footfall-lore-bastianrook-1-choice = What does the kitchen give Footfall besides food?
wh40k-footfall-lore-bastianrook-1-reply = A reason to stop. The docks always have someone's urgent voyage; here you can sit a few minutes and remember the day belongs to you too. We are no great House or order. Dinner simply needs to be ready before the next shift.
wh40k-footfall-lore-bastianrook-2-choice = What is hardest about a port kitchen?
wh40k-footfall-lore-bastianrook-2-reply = Finding out how many people will actually arrive. A captain says 'small crew' and every sailor brings a friend. I trust a full table more than the advance request. The table at least never insists it is only slightly hungry.

wh40k-footfall-lore-adrianvey-1-choice = How is the port medicae service organised?
wh40k-footfall-lore-adrianvey-1-reply = Doctors receive patients, suppliers keep stock, and duty staff hand over records. The charter defines obligations; a shift's work treats the patient, not its seal. Everyone has a part. If everyone assumes someone else's part matters more, a person is left between desks.
wh40k-footfall-lore-adrianvey-2-choice = What do you want to hear from a patient?
wh40k-footfall-lore-adrianvey-2-reply = What happened, when, and what they have tried already. Not every way they might have managed without us. Those lists are usually longer than the clinical history. I need to understand the condition, not win an argument with their pride.

wh40k-footfall-lore-mirafenn-1-choice = Why does the dispensary belong to medicae?
wh40k-footfall-lore-mirafenn-1-reply = Consumable stocks are part of the same service as receiving patients. Batches need records, issues need care, and doctors need to know what remains. I prefer good stockkeeping to handsome promises. A promise will not hold a dressing in place.
wh40k-footfall-lore-mirafenn-2-choice = Do you often argue with customers?
wh40k-footfall-lore-mirafenn-2-reply = Usually with people following a neighbour's confidence as medical advice. I can show the stock, but a counter conversation does not replace a doctor. Footfall loves retelling others' feats. It retells others' prescriptions just as readily and rather less successfully.

wh40k-footfall-lore-quarantineofficer-1-choice = Why guard quarantine?
wh40k-footfall-lore-quarantineofficer-1-reply = Medicae answer for those still well as well as the patient. I keep the ward boundary and pass requests to doctors. It is easy to look unfriendly at this door. It is worse to let one hurried visit become the whole shift's problem.
wh40k-footfall-lore-quarantineofficer-2-choice = What do you expect from a visitor?
wh40k-footfall-lore-quarantineofficer-2-reply = Ask first, then enter if permission is given. Every 'just for a minute' seems remarkably sure of the way around the duty officer. I do not argue with good intentions. I ask them to wait this side of the door until the doctor answers.

wh40k-footfall-lore-chartistmerchant-1-choice = How does Chartist trade differ from Rogue Trade?
wh40k-footfall-lore-chartistmerchant-1-reply = The Merchant Charter binds our fleet to established routes and obligations. A Rogue Trader may seek a new passage; Chartists maintain the regular carriage. My batches tell more of a macro-transport's long work than sudden discoveries. But they have actually arrived.
wh40k-footfall-lore-chartistmerchant-2-choice = What do you appreciate in port customers?
wh40k-footfall-lore-chartistmerchant-2-reply = Precise orders and meeting a cargo on time. Sailors spend much of their lives between sailing and unloading; here they can see who needed what they carried. Nicer than another letter insisting the ship should have travelled faster.

wh40k-footfall-lore-cryopriest-1-choice = Why is a priest stationed by the sleep arks?
wh40k-footfall-lore-cryopriest-1-reply = The Ecclesiarchy accompanies people before long waits as well as long journeys. Some fear the sleep, others the world awaiting them. I help them gather their thoughts and offer prayer. They must still await the ark's confirmation: a blessing does not certify a lock.
wh40k-footfall-lore-cryopriest-2-choice = What do people discuss before a long sleep?
wh40k-footfall-lore-cryopriest-2-reply = Most often the ordinary words they never said to someone. A person can prepare for a star voyage and be lost before a short farewell. Speak beforehand if you can. The ark keeps the body; someone else will have to keep the unsaid words.

wh40k-footfall-lore-fizzo-1-choice = Why do so many people gather at your counter?
wh40k-footfall-lore-fizzo-1-reply = A ship divides people into watches; a counter sometimes brings them together. A docker, trader and crew member can order a drink without explaining their whole rank. Footfall needs that more than another office. It is much more interesting for a bartender too.
wh40k-footfall-lore-fizzo-2-choice = Which rumours do you trust?
wh40k-footfall-lore-fizzo-2-reply = Those whose beginnings can be traced, not merely their loud endings. I hear who waited for passage, who returned and who is trying to look as though they did. A counter conversation remains a conversation. Check before building an expedition, accusation or family quarrel upon it.
